1
00:01:42,901 --> 00:01:44,368
Oh my goodness!

2
00:01:45,402 --> 00:01:47,871
Did you crash here last night?

3
00:01:51,275 --> 00:01:52,495
My apologies.

4
00:01:52,495 --> 00:01:55,145
You gotta quit boozing
with the undergrads until dawn.

5
00:01:55,145 --> 00:01:56,636
You hit the big three-oh, didn't you?

6
00:01:56,636 --> 00:01:58,682
Stop acting like a child.

7
00:01:58,682 --> 00:02:00,136
Wait, where did it go?

8
00:02:00,136 --> 00:02:02,185
Did you happen to see a red USB anywhere?

9
00:02:02,686 --> 00:02:03,587
Excuse me?

10
00:02:03,587 --> 00:02:05,234
My red USB.

11
00:02:05,234 --> 00:02:06,223
Well...

12
00:02:06,223 --> 00:02:08,292
I'm in a rush right now.

13
00:02:08,292 --> 00:02:09,759
Just track it down for me, will you?

14
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,228
On it.

15
00:02:11,228 --> 00:02:14,098
And if you get a chance, tidy up this pigsty.

16
00:02:14,098 --> 00:02:16,368
What a mess.

17
00:02:16,368 --> 00:02:19,536
Don't you think
it's time you got your act together?

18
00:02:21,175 --> 00:02:23,040
Professor.

19
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,274
Yeah?

20
00:02:26,935 --> 00:02:29,746
Do you recall what you told me a while back?

21
00:02:31,055 --> 00:02:32,716
Huh? What did I say?

22
00:02:35,223 --> 00:02:37,854
You asked if I even cared about my own future.

23
00:02:38,322 --> 00:02:40,924
And you said I was sabotaging my own life.

24
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:45,996
I said that?

25
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:48,432
That was a little rough. My bad.

26
00:02:48,432 --> 00:02:50,100
Professor, I...

27
00:02:52,234 --> 00:02:55,272
I'm done being a detriment to myself.

28
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:57,942
I've started caring a lot

29
00:02:57,942 --> 00:02:59,476
about my life.

30
00:03:31,609 --> 00:03:33,076
Hey there.

31
00:03:34,078 --> 00:03:35,846
Same old, same old with me.

32
00:03:35,846 --> 00:03:37,514
Have you been keeping well?

33
00:03:39,142 --> 00:03:40,350
What?

34
00:03:42,077 --> 00:03:43,701
I feel...

35
00:03:43,701 --> 00:03:45,956
perfectly healthy,
but the doctors insist it's cancer.

36
00:03:46,724 --> 00:03:49,042
You seem so fit, though.

37
00:03:49,042 --> 00:03:51,022
Exactly.

38
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:53,264
What you don't know can't hurt you.

39
00:03:53,264 --> 00:03:55,478
Knowing is the real sickness.

40
00:03:55,478 --> 00:03:56,366
Hey.

41
00:03:56,366 --> 00:03:59,558
I don't even feel that cheated.

42
00:03:59,558 --> 00:04:01,105
Given how old I am,

43
00:04:01,105 --> 00:04:03,874
and all the booze and cigarettes
I've consumed over the years.

44
00:04:08,646 --> 00:04:11,248
- Please, help yourselves to these.
- Thank you.

45
00:04:12,249 --> 00:04:14,151
Honey, drink this.

46
00:04:15,219 --> 00:04:16,920
Aren't you freezing?

47
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,589
Do you really think I'd be cold
wearing all these layers in this weather?

48
00:04:18,589 --> 00:04:21,425
Oh, catching a cold would be a disaster.

49
00:04:21,425 --> 00:04:22,860
Let me go grab a blanket.

50
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,892
Just keep this on.

51
00:04:24,892 --> 00:04:26,596
I'm roasting.

52
00:04:28,632 --> 00:04:30,867
I'll be back in a minute.

53
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:38,509
Even my youngest finally got a job,

54
00:04:38,509 --> 00:04:41,905
and the kids have been sending us
more than enough pocket money.

55
00:04:41,905 --> 00:04:44,972
I was supposed to be seeing
the world with my wife.

56
00:04:44,972 --> 00:04:47,617
But instead, I end up
with this useless illness.

57
00:04:49,259 --> 00:04:51,722
Last year when we went on that trip,

58
00:04:51,722 --> 00:04:55,459
my wife wanted to use her miles
to upgrade to business class.

59
00:04:55,459 --> 00:04:58,342
I said no because it felt wasteful,
but I really regret it now.

60
00:04:58,342 --> 00:05:01,097
Just get better soon, then go.

61
00:05:02,533 --> 00:05:04,529
Do you think I'll ever get to use those miles?

62
00:05:04,529 --> 00:05:06,170
Of course.

63
00:05:06,170 --> 00:05:08,806
- You have to use them.
- Why say things like that?

64
00:05:08,806 --> 00:05:10,541
Right.

65
00:05:10,541 --> 00:05:13,630
I gotta heal up and travel like crazy.

66
00:05:13,630 --> 00:05:15,145
No regrets.

67
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:27,234
I know I shouldn't say this,

68
00:05:27,234 --> 00:05:29,280
but rather than the patient,

69
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:33,496
I worry more about the guardian.

70
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:38,468
They're such cheerful people, though.

71
00:05:38,468 --> 00:05:40,704
They'll overcome this just fine.

72
00:05:44,741 --> 00:05:47,400
I heard someone wrote this

73
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:49,346
on their tombstone.

74
00:05:50,914 --> 00:05:53,033
"I knew this would happen

75
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:55,085
while I was hesitating."

76
00:05:57,103 --> 00:06:00,190
I swore I wouldn't live like that,

77
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:02,434
but I was wishy-washy again.

78
00:06:02,434 --> 00:06:04,527
I kept dragging my feet.

79
00:06:07,264 --> 00:06:09,633
I'll live my life my way

80
00:06:10,334 --> 00:06:13,057
and the kids will figure theirs out.

81
00:06:13,057 --> 00:06:15,133
I'm going to make sure...

82
00:06:15,133 --> 00:06:17,073
I live a happy life, no matter what.

83
00:06:28,352 --> 00:06:30,487
Father, are you looking for something?

84
00:06:30,487 --> 00:06:33,326
Do you know where our tent went?

85
00:06:33,326 --> 00:06:34,607
The tent?

86
00:06:34,607 --> 00:06:35,892
Yeah.

87
00:06:36,894 --> 00:06:39,262
The one for the retreat.

88
00:06:43,634 --> 00:06:46,697
If things had worked out with Jun Kyung,

89
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:49,567
I wouldn't have stood by like this
as a brother-in-law.

90
00:06:49,567 --> 00:06:50,753
Man.

91
00:06:50,753 --> 00:06:52,849
You're lucky I chose the priesthood over love.

92
00:06:52,849 --> 00:06:55,446
That's the only reason you're still alive.

93
00:06:55,446 --> 00:06:57,247
Anyway, thank you.

94
00:06:57,965 --> 00:07:00,425
Just return it before the summer retreat.

95
00:07:00,425 --> 00:07:02,366
Not that I expect you to last that long.

96
00:07:02,366 --> 00:07:04,521
I'll bring it back by then.

97
00:07:05,725 --> 00:07:07,390
Seriously, I will! Okay?

98
00:07:08,458 --> 00:07:10,961
I'm definitely bringing it back.

99
00:07:10,961 --> 00:07:13,597
Man, your dad is already worried sick...

100
00:07:13,597 --> 00:07:16,005
I wonder if I'm making a mistake here.

101
00:07:16,005 --> 00:07:17,463
Hey.

102
00:07:18,834 --> 00:07:21,605
You seriously can't tell Dad.

103
00:07:21,605 --> 00:07:23,940
Treat this like the seal of the confessional.

104
00:07:25,585 --> 00:07:28,311
It's a promise to the guy
who almost became your brother-in-law.

105
00:07:29,513 --> 00:07:30,816
Hurry up.

106
00:07:33,083 --> 00:07:34,584
There we go.

107
00:07:38,221 --> 00:07:40,490
You really can't say a word.

108
00:07:41,584 --> 00:07:43,360
Swear to God.

109
00:07:49,533 --> 00:07:51,801
You're the reason I came back.

110
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:54,871
I wanted to give us another shot.

111
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:44,454
Do you think this might be too much for her?

112
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:49,159
I've never seen a woman
feel burdened by a diamond.

113
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:52,429
Usually, it's the men who feel the burden.

114
00:08:52,429 --> 00:08:56,233
The woman getting this will surely be happy.

115
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:59,520
Sincerity is what really makes a woman happy.

116
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:02,406
And if that man is capable,

117
00:09:02,406 --> 00:09:05,542
it brings her a little extra joy.

118
00:09:11,362 --> 00:09:13,716
What did I do so wrong?

119
00:09:15,752 --> 00:09:18,747
I worked myself to the bone
to earn that money...

120
00:09:18,747 --> 00:09:21,791
I'm selling the house I bought
with my own sweat and tears...

121
00:09:23,427 --> 00:09:26,133
All I'm saying is I want to pursue
my own happiness now.

122
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:28,498
Do I deserve all this hate for that?

123
00:09:34,571 --> 00:09:37,006
What's weighing on your mind?

124
00:09:38,408 --> 00:09:41,010
You always go for a walk
when you've got a lot on your mind.

125
00:09:41,635 --> 00:09:44,714
But isn't walking all the way home
a bit excessive?

126
00:09:46,316 --> 00:09:48,716
Jun Kyung, hop in. Hurry.

127
00:09:48,716 --> 00:09:50,487
I'm sorry.

128
00:09:53,615 --> 00:09:55,220
Even if it's his house,

129
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,861
I don't get why Dad wants
to sell it out of the blue.

130
00:09:57,861 --> 00:09:58,991
And I don't get Jun Seo,

131
00:09:58,991 --> 00:10:01,998
losing his temper when it's not even his house.

132
00:10:02,732 --> 00:10:05,969
Seriously, they're grown adults.
What is their problem?

133
00:10:08,205 --> 00:10:10,874
I think I kind of get it.

134
00:10:12,776 --> 00:10:14,944
Since when are you so understanding?

135
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,050
Not just understanding, honestly, I'm envious.

136
00:10:20,050 --> 00:10:21,038
Of what?

137
00:10:21,038 --> 00:10:22,586
Your father.

138
00:10:22,586 --> 00:10:25,568
Making such a bold decision

139
00:10:25,568 --> 00:10:28,658
for the person he loves...

140
00:10:29,734 --> 00:10:31,628
I think that's cool.

141
00:10:31,628 --> 00:10:33,558
Where can you find a man like that?

142
00:10:33,558 --> 00:10:36,498
He's not just a man. He's a father.

143
00:10:36,498 --> 00:10:38,835
You moved out.

144
00:10:38,835 --> 00:10:42,895
Jun Seo is barely home
between school and dating.

145
00:10:43,651 --> 00:10:45,408
Since your father is home alone,

146
00:10:45,408 --> 00:10:47,244
I think he might feel that way.

147
00:10:47,244 --> 00:10:49,192
Then she could just move in and live with him.

148
00:10:49,192 --> 00:10:50,752
Do you think she'd be comfortable with that?

149
00:10:50,752 --> 00:10:53,049
Jun Seo wouldn't be comfortable either.

150
00:10:59,290 --> 00:11:01,292
Why?

151
00:11:01,292 --> 00:11:04,861
This is why I like you.

152
00:11:13,064 --> 00:11:15,672
Being a father, being a man...

153
00:11:18,300 --> 00:11:20,777
I'm not good at it either. It's hard.

154
00:11:23,046 --> 00:11:24,881
It is hard.

155
00:11:26,016 --> 00:11:28,925
I've been moved out for a while

156
00:11:28,925 --> 00:11:32,255
and thought that house
didn't mean much to me...

157
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:36,593
But now that I think about it disappearing,

158
00:11:36,593 --> 00:11:38,728
I feel a bit weird.

159
00:11:47,537 --> 00:11:50,040
You've maintained it really well, huh?

160
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,062
For its age,

161
00:11:51,062 --> 00:11:54,678
the floors and molding are pristine.

162
00:11:54,678 --> 00:11:57,297
Anyone could move in
and start living here right away.

163
00:11:57,297 --> 00:11:58,555
Oh, really?

164
00:11:58,555 --> 00:12:00,884
It's my first time selling a house.

165
00:12:00,884 --> 00:12:02,770
I envy you.

166
00:12:02,770 --> 00:12:04,877
Even if it's your first time, you're selling.

167
00:12:04,877 --> 00:12:07,824
I don't even have a house to sell.

168
00:12:12,363 --> 00:12:13,868
No.

169
00:12:13,868 --> 00:12:17,300
You have to pan with your phone

170
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:20,043
from here to make it look wider.

171
00:12:20,043 --> 00:12:21,438
Gosh, I've told you a million times.

172
00:12:21,438 --> 00:12:22,734
Excuse me.

173
00:12:22,734 --> 00:12:24,743
How long do you think
it'll take to sell the house?

174
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:26,483
Ah, well...

175
00:12:26,483 --> 00:12:28,166
You'd be surprised how many people are looking

176
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:30,614
for a house with a yard like this these days.

177
00:12:30,614 --> 00:12:33,450
It's great for raising kids and keeping dogs.

178
00:12:33,450 --> 00:12:36,163
A property like this
could sell as early as tomorrow.

179
00:12:36,163 --> 00:12:37,454
Oh...

180
00:12:37,454 --> 00:12:39,191
The photos and videos we took today

181
00:12:39,191 --> 00:12:41,425
will be uploaded to our blog immediately.

182
00:12:41,425 --> 00:12:42,774
That fast?

183
00:12:42,774 --> 00:12:43,615
Hey,

184
00:12:43,615 --> 00:12:47,096
we gotta be fast
to survive in this day and age.

185
00:12:49,801 --> 00:12:51,133
Over there.

186
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:53,002
Yeah, just like that.

187
00:12:54,571 --> 00:12:56,307
Is it guaranteed?

188
00:12:56,307 --> 00:12:58,114
Did he say he'd give you the lecturer position?

189
00:12:58,114 --> 00:13:01,411
It's not officially decided yet,

190
00:13:02,913 --> 00:13:05,434
but he said he'd definitely recommend me.

191
00:13:05,434 --> 00:13:07,071
He trusts me.

192
00:13:07,071 --> 00:13:09,987
Why would he trust a guy who's still in school

193
00:13:09,987 --> 00:13:12,221
because he couldn't get enough credits?

194
00:13:13,958 --> 00:13:15,892
Your patience and persistence?

195
00:13:18,428 --> 00:13:19,997
Right?

196
00:13:19,997 --> 00:13:22,165
That's a great talent, too.

197
00:13:24,167 --> 00:13:26,033
By the way,

198
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:29,672
you criticized your dad for selling
the house without consulting you,

199
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:33,165
but now you're building a house here
without consulting me?

200
00:13:33,165 --> 00:13:36,880
I'm just saying
we should share this leftover land.

201
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:40,150
And share some of your food, too.

202
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,753
And as for the bathroom...

203
00:13:42,753 --> 00:13:44,308
maybe I can use it when you're not?

204
00:13:44,308 --> 00:13:46,156
Hey, once I become a lecturer,

205
00:13:46,156 --> 00:13:48,253
I'm leaving right away, even if you cry

206
00:13:48,253 --> 00:13:49,893
and beg me not to go because you're lonely.

207
00:13:49,893 --> 00:13:52,048
So don't worry.

208
00:13:52,048 --> 00:13:53,463
Oh, boy.

209
00:13:58,802 --> 00:14:00,536
But tell me,

210
00:14:01,033 --> 00:14:03,736
did you actually want to become a lecturer?

211
00:14:03,736 --> 00:14:05,208
As of today,

212
00:14:05,208 --> 00:14:08,167
I have been reborn as a man

213
00:14:08,167 --> 00:14:10,147
born to be a lecturer.

214
00:14:10,147 --> 00:14:11,529
Why?

215
00:14:11,529 --> 00:14:13,089
Because I need to avenge

216
00:14:13,089 --> 00:14:15,474
the humiliation and insults
I received from my dad and sister.

217
00:14:18,405 --> 00:14:20,658
You must not tell anyone I'm here.

218
00:14:20,658 --> 00:14:21,991
Got it?

219
00:14:23,961 --> 00:14:25,428
Got it?

220
00:14:27,228 --> 00:14:30,300
Jun Seo is at my place.

221
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:33,436
I thought you and Jin Ho might be worried.

222
00:14:37,674 --> 00:14:38,809
I know.

223
00:14:38,809 --> 00:14:41,145
How did you know?

224
00:14:41,145 --> 00:14:43,113
The priest told me.

225
00:14:43,113 --> 00:14:44,835
Chang Sik?

226
00:14:44,835 --> 00:14:46,783
How did he know?

227
00:14:46,783 --> 00:14:48,084
I'm not going to worry anymore either.

228
00:14:48,084 --> 00:14:49,536
Jun Seo will figure it out.

229
00:14:49,536 --> 00:14:52,356
As you said, he isn't a kid.

230
00:14:52,356 --> 00:14:54,267
And

231
00:14:54,267 --> 00:14:56,325
I put the house on the market.

232
00:14:57,828 --> 00:14:59,295
Just so you know.

233
00:15:01,788 --> 00:15:03,099
Okay.

234
00:15:13,243 --> 00:15:14,621
- Hello.
- Hello.

235
00:15:14,621 --> 00:15:16,546
Yes, please come in.

236
00:15:16,546 --> 00:15:18,100
- Please come in.
- Excuse us.

237
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,416
- Hello.
- Hi.

238
00:15:19,416 --> 00:15:21,101
We'll start by looking inside.

239
00:15:21,101 --> 00:15:23,888
- Yes, go ahead. Take your time.
- Thank you.

240
00:15:23,888 --> 00:15:25,521
Let's go this way.

241
00:15:34,567 --> 00:15:35,532
Here,

242
00:15:35,532 --> 00:15:37,500
please have some of this
while you take your time looking around.

243
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:38,935
Thank you.

244
00:15:38,935 --> 00:15:40,736
Thank you.

245
00:15:41,905 --> 00:15:44,267
It's a lot more run-down

246
00:15:44,267 --> 00:15:46,253
than it looked in the video.

247
00:15:46,253 --> 00:15:48,578
It's really old-fashioned, isn't it?

248
00:15:49,473 --> 00:15:51,634
When we redo the wallpaper and floors,

249
00:15:51,634 --> 00:15:54,118
we should change all the doors, too.

250
00:15:54,118 --> 00:15:56,085
Of course, you should change them.

251
00:15:59,652 --> 00:16:02,459
Judging by your fashion,
you two have great taste,

252
00:16:02,459 --> 00:16:04,828
so I bet you'll decorate the house beautifully.

253
00:17:44,627 --> 00:17:47,746
The living room is a bit small
for the square footage.

254
00:17:47,746 --> 00:17:51,033
Since you said you only need a nursery
and one other room,

255
00:17:51,506 --> 00:17:54,572
you could just knock down this wall
to combine the rooms.

256
00:17:54,572 --> 00:17:55,871
Is it safe

257
00:17:58,274 --> 00:17:59,657
to knock the wall down?

258
00:17:59,657 --> 00:18:01,620
Old houses are sturdier.

259
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,046
It's built like a tank, a total tank.

260
00:18:03,046 --> 00:18:04,814
Just knock it all down.

261
00:18:08,934 --> 00:18:11,558
Won't there be too many bugs in the summer?

262
00:18:11,558 --> 00:18:13,501
We don't need a vegetable garden anyway.

263
00:18:13,501 --> 00:18:15,258
Should we install a deck over here?

264
00:18:15,258 --> 00:18:17,568
Yeah, if you put in a deck

265
00:18:17,568 --> 00:18:19,663
and set up a parasol,

266
00:18:19,663 --> 00:18:21,665
you won't need to go to a cafe.

267
00:18:24,233 --> 00:18:25,802
Hey, look.

268
00:18:25,802 --> 00:18:27,467
If you don't like the house,
you don't have to buy it.

269
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:29,354
Why are you spouting nonsense
about tearing down

270
00:18:29,354 --> 00:18:30,406
and renovating someone else's home?

271
00:18:30,406 --> 00:18:32,067
Mr. Seo,

272
00:18:32,067 --> 00:18:35,390
they're just trying to make it even better
because they like it.

273
00:18:35,390 --> 00:18:37,982
This guy is ridiculous.

274
00:18:37,982 --> 00:18:39,250
I'm ridiculous?

275
00:18:39,250 --> 00:18:40,750
What's ridiculous about me?

276
00:18:40,750 --> 00:18:42,853
I think you two are the ridiculous ones.

277
00:18:42,853 --> 00:18:44,621
You have no idea what kind of house this is.

278
00:18:44,621 --> 00:18:46,255
I'm not selling, so get out.

279
00:18:46,255 --> 00:18:47,791
I think there's a misunderstanding.

280
00:18:47,791 --> 00:18:50,593
And you're the worst! Seriously!

281
00:18:50,593 --> 00:18:52,111
You said it didn't need any work.

282
00:18:52,111 --> 00:18:52,911
Get out.

283
00:18:52,911 --> 00:18:53,771
I'm not selling to you, so get out.

284
00:18:53,771 --> 00:18:55,135
Hurry up and get out.

285
00:18:55,135 --> 00:18:56,232
- Get out.
- Mr. Seo.

286
00:18:56,232 --> 00:18:57,567
Get out!

287
00:18:57,567 --> 00:18:58,256
Mr. Seo?

288
00:18:58,256 --> 00:19:00,004
Ah, yes.

289
00:19:00,004 --> 00:19:01,475
I think it went well.

290
00:19:01,475 --> 00:19:03,235
I'll be in touch.

291
00:19:03,235 --> 00:19:04,795
Okay.

292
00:19:04,795 --> 00:19:05,656
Yes, okay.

293
00:19:05,656 --> 00:19:06,915
Let's go.

294
00:19:06,915 --> 00:19:08,677
Thanks for showing us the house.

295
00:19:19,022 --> 00:19:20,689
Did my mom

296
00:19:21,524 --> 00:19:25,628
make a mistake with you that day?

297
00:19:26,236 --> 00:19:27,696
No.

298
00:19:29,266 --> 00:19:31,634
She probably did.

299
00:19:33,688 --> 00:19:35,671
But please

300
00:19:36,534 --> 00:19:39,175
don't hate her too much.

301
00:19:40,244 --> 00:19:42,278
I don't.

302
00:19:45,114 --> 00:19:47,116
Since I'm gone now,

303
00:19:47,116 --> 00:19:48,584
you don't have to walk on eggshells.

304
00:19:48,584 --> 00:19:50,816
Feel free to sleep over at my dad's place.

305
00:19:50,816 --> 00:19:53,255
You sound like you're
never going to see me again.

306
00:19:54,325 --> 00:19:56,325
Why wouldn't I?

307
00:19:57,218 --> 00:19:59,095
If you break up

308
00:19:59,734 --> 00:20:01,634
with my dad,

309
00:20:01,634 --> 00:20:04,001
will you stop seeing me?

310
00:20:04,001 --> 00:20:05,301
What?

311
00:20:06,133 --> 00:20:07,470
I mean,

312
00:20:08,137 --> 00:20:10,300
you never know with people.

313
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:11,574
Not that

314
00:20:11,574 --> 00:20:14,310
I want you to break up.

315
00:20:14,911 --> 00:20:16,579
My dad

316
00:20:19,434 --> 00:20:21,684
is a pretty decent guy.

317
00:20:23,664 --> 00:20:26,556
Wow, your Korean has really improved.

318
00:20:26,556 --> 00:20:29,258
You can say just about anything now.

319
00:20:48,411 --> 00:20:50,272
You brought the fish, too?

320
00:20:50,272 --> 00:20:51,982
Oh...

321
00:20:51,982 --> 00:20:53,215
yeah.

322
00:20:53,783 --> 00:20:55,586
Why? Do you hate it?

323
00:20:55,586 --> 00:20:56,723
No.

324
00:20:56,723 --> 00:20:58,120
Let's go inside.

325
00:21:08,866 --> 00:21:10,263
I'm leaving.

326
00:21:10,263 --> 00:21:11,202
Good luck unpacking.

327
00:21:11,202 --> 00:21:12,303
What?

328
00:21:12,303 --> 00:21:14,637
You expect Daniel and me
to carry all this by ourselves?

329
00:21:15,806 --> 00:21:17,942
It's not that much stuff.

330
00:21:17,942 --> 00:21:20,009
You're not recording today, are you?

331
00:21:21,077 --> 00:21:24,597
It's not like you're forbidden to be here,
so stay for dinner.

332
00:21:24,597 --> 00:21:26,137
You like curry.

333
00:21:26,137 --> 00:21:27,897
I actually put some effort
into cooking for once.

334
00:21:27,897 --> 00:21:29,685
I'm meeting Jun Kyung.

335
00:21:35,759 --> 00:21:37,717
Okay, then.

336
00:21:37,717 --> 00:21:40,337
I won't rush you.

337
00:21:40,337 --> 00:21:43,667
We'll have to see each other anyway
because of Daniel.

338
00:21:43,667 --> 00:21:45,434
I have plenty of time.

339
00:21:46,136 --> 00:21:47,536
I'm going.

340
00:22:54,218 --> 00:22:55,938
Yeah, Jun Seo.

341
00:22:57,041 --> 00:22:58,641
Are you going to be late again?

342
00:22:59,221 --> 00:23:01,644
Gosh, you're working so hard.

343
00:23:01,644 --> 00:23:03,779
Okay, make sure you eat something.

344
00:23:04,303 --> 00:23:05,797
Okay.

345
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:21,300
When I was little,

346
00:24:21,300 --> 00:24:23,893
Mom would always bring in the laundry

347
00:24:23,893 --> 00:24:26,362
and fold it on the living room floor

348
00:24:27,133 --> 00:24:29,665
right around this time.

349
00:24:30,434 --> 00:24:34,470
I would always sit next to her and help.

350
00:24:35,224 --> 00:24:38,340
Even though I did a terrible, messy job,

351
00:24:38,862 --> 00:24:41,712
Mom would say, "You're such a good boy.

352
00:24:41,712 --> 00:24:44,012
You're doing a great job."

353
00:24:44,962 --> 00:24:46,715
Then

354
00:24:47,267 --> 00:24:49,151
Jun Kyung would come home from school.

355
00:24:49,982 --> 00:24:52,054
A little later,

356
00:24:53,434 --> 00:24:56,291
Dad would come home from work.

357
00:24:57,193 --> 00:25:00,896
Then we'd all have dinner together,

358
00:25:01,643 --> 00:25:05,634
and eat ice cream because Mom loved it so much.

359
00:25:06,801 --> 00:25:08,971
That's a nice memory.

360
00:25:10,639 --> 00:25:13,075
Our family was really happy back then.

361
00:25:27,934 --> 00:25:29,133
Hello?

362
00:25:29,133 --> 00:25:30,901
It's me.

363
00:25:30,901 --> 00:25:32,761
Are you done already?

364
00:25:34,067 --> 00:25:37,233
You must be sad after sending Daniel off.

365
00:25:37,233 --> 00:25:38,834
I am.

366
00:25:38,834 --> 00:25:41,603
When I go home, Daniel won't be there,

367
00:25:42,133 --> 00:25:43,774
Oscar won't be there...

368
00:25:43,774 --> 00:25:46,057
The only moving thing in that house

369
00:25:46,057 --> 00:25:48,577
will be the robot vacuum.

370
00:25:53,182 --> 00:25:55,611
Maybe I should give up the place.

371
00:25:55,611 --> 00:25:57,634
The lease is ending anyway.

372
00:25:57,634 --> 00:25:59,356
I should find a spot that fits me better,

373
00:25:59,356 --> 00:26:02,424
something meant for living solo.

374
00:26:07,701 --> 00:26:09,631
Where are you right now?

375
00:26:12,097 --> 00:26:15,606
I'm at my dad's, but the place is empty.

376
00:26:15,606 --> 00:26:18,157
What are you doing there all by yourself?

377
00:26:18,157 --> 00:26:19,708
Just...

378
00:26:20,634 --> 00:26:22,377
sitting.

379
00:26:27,926 --> 00:26:30,285
Being here alone...

380
00:26:31,345 --> 00:26:34,456
I get where my dad is coming from,
just like you said.

381
00:26:35,337 --> 00:26:38,961
I don't think I can object
even if he sells the place now.

382
00:26:42,995 --> 00:26:44,500
Jun Kyung.

383
00:26:45,236 --> 00:26:46,502
Yeah?

384
00:26:48,606 --> 00:26:50,506
How about we move in together?

385
00:26:54,499 --> 00:26:56,846
Those people really crossed the line.

386
00:26:56,846 --> 00:27:00,015
I mean, who trash-talks a house
right in front of the owner?

387
00:27:00,015 --> 00:27:02,117
It offended me just listening to it.

388
00:27:04,578 --> 00:27:08,791
Who's going to praise a place
when the owner puts it on the market

389
00:27:08,791 --> 00:27:10,959
like it means nothing to him?

390
00:27:11,632 --> 00:27:14,064
Clearing out Bom's spot felt so wrong,

391
00:27:14,064 --> 00:27:18,033
like I was erasing all the time
we spent together.

392
00:27:22,238 --> 00:27:24,907
But it's not like we're doing this

393
00:27:24,907 --> 00:27:28,477
because we don't cherish it.

394
00:27:34,083 --> 00:27:35,884
Hang on.

395
00:27:40,724 --> 00:27:42,291
Hello?

396
00:27:46,206 --> 00:27:47,592
[Seo Jun Kyung]

397
00:27:47,592 --> 00:27:48,897
What?

398
00:27:55,339 --> 00:27:56,874
You scared me!

399
00:27:56,874 --> 00:27:58,732
Why aren't you picking up my calls?

400
00:27:58,732 --> 00:28:00,444
How did you find me here?

401
00:28:00,444 --> 00:28:02,444
Is your location some kind of top-secret intel?

402
00:28:04,647 --> 00:28:05,612
What?

403
00:28:05,612 --> 00:28:08,992
Seriously, I can't trust anyone.

404
00:28:08,992 --> 00:28:10,354
You can't tell Dad. It's a secret.

405
00:28:10,354 --> 00:28:12,917
Dad already knows.

406
00:28:14,505 --> 00:28:16,224
You told him?

407
00:28:17,309 --> 00:28:19,949
Did you not hear me say he already knows?

408
00:28:19,949 --> 00:28:22,749
Ah, it was Chang Sik!

409
00:28:22,749 --> 00:28:25,903
How does a priest have such a big mouth?

410
00:28:25,903 --> 00:28:28,270
Just come out.

411
00:28:29,773 --> 00:28:31,440
Where are we headed?

412
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:35,277
You have to tell me.

413
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:38,180
Isn't Do Hyun's idea amazing?

414
00:28:38,180 --> 00:28:41,817
If he and I clear out our places
and rent this house,

415
00:28:41,817 --> 00:28:43,734
we won't have to sell it.

416
00:28:43,734 --> 00:28:46,455
Dad, you can run the campsite with Ja Yeong,

417
00:28:46,455 --> 00:28:48,893
and Jun Seo can stay in his room.

418
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:50,227
No way.

419
00:28:50,227 --> 00:28:52,138
Why should I mooch off you?

420
00:28:52,138 --> 00:28:54,096
You stubborn rascal.

421
00:28:54,096 --> 00:28:56,119
I'm absolutely going to become independent
on my own this time.

422
00:28:56,119 --> 00:28:59,868
Knock it off. Don't be a burden to Hye On.

423
00:28:59,868 --> 00:29:01,219
He's not a burden.

424
00:29:01,219 --> 00:29:04,840
It's actually reassuring
having Jun Seo around...

425
00:29:06,010 --> 00:29:08,244
Well, maybe not exactly.

426
00:29:08,244 --> 00:29:11,549
But he works as a free bodyguard,

427
00:29:11,549 --> 00:29:13,115
so I like it.

428
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:19,860
What is your opinion?

429
00:29:19,860 --> 00:29:23,140
Do I get a say in this?

430
00:29:23,140 --> 00:29:24,520
Of course.

431
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:27,281
We don't have to put the house on the market,

432
00:29:27,281 --> 00:29:29,540
so I'm totally down with that.

433
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:30,832
Right?

434
00:29:31,435 --> 00:29:34,480
But are you seriously okay with this?

435
00:29:34,480 --> 00:29:36,840
You might be love-struck right now,

436
00:29:36,840 --> 00:29:39,194
but that bubble is going to burst eventually.

437
00:29:39,194 --> 00:29:41,745
What's the plan for this house
when money gets in the mix?

438
00:29:41,745 --> 00:29:42,980
I'm all for it.

439
00:29:42,980 --> 00:29:45,147
If the property prevents us
from splitting up, that's a bonus.

440
00:29:54,458 --> 00:29:56,191
What do you think, Dad?

441
00:30:08,871 --> 00:30:10,439
Dad?

442
00:30:11,734 --> 00:30:13,275
I think...

443
00:30:20,067 --> 00:30:22,250
If you guys think so...

444
00:30:31,593 --> 00:30:34,265
Is Dad still pouting?

445
00:30:34,265 --> 00:30:37,265
Is he acting like a baby or what?

446
00:30:37,265 --> 00:30:40,202
One more peep out of you,
and I'll stitch those lips together.

447
00:30:47,334 --> 00:30:49,177
What's the matter?

448
00:31:03,158 --> 00:31:04,893
This house isn't

449
00:31:05,601 --> 00:31:08,263
just about my past.

450
00:31:09,634 --> 00:31:12,167
It holds your history,

451
00:31:12,167 --> 00:31:14,669
Jun Seo's,

452
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:18,740
and Mi Ran's, too. It belongs to all of us.

453
00:31:20,609 --> 00:31:23,278
I've been so self-centered and pathetic.

454
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:27,382
I can't even face you guys.

455
00:31:36,827 --> 00:31:38,794
No.

456
00:31:40,467 --> 00:31:42,597
The day we first moved in,

457
00:31:43,639 --> 00:31:46,216
I asked myself if we were worthy
of such a fine home.

458
00:31:46,216 --> 00:31:47,915
I couldn't sleep a wink,

459
00:31:47,915 --> 00:31:49,704
especially after barely scraping by
on monthly rent.

460
00:31:50,841 --> 00:31:53,575
Mom really cherished this place.

461
00:31:55,002 --> 00:31:58,947
Your mom and I were so fond of this house.

462
00:31:58,947 --> 00:32:01,834
We upgraded from a monthly rent
to a full deposit lease,

463
00:32:01,834 --> 00:32:04,152
and finally, we made it ours.

464
00:32:04,860 --> 00:32:08,323
We both bawled our eyes out that night.

465
00:32:13,529 --> 00:32:17,165
Think about how frugal your mom
had to be during that time,

466
00:32:18,135 --> 00:32:20,302
and how hard she struggled.

467
00:32:20,969 --> 00:32:23,467
She had Jun Seo here,

468
00:32:23,467 --> 00:32:25,407
raised you,

469
00:32:27,133 --> 00:32:29,477
and supported me, too.

470
00:32:35,619 --> 00:32:37,103
Hey.

471
00:32:38,086 --> 00:32:40,322
Your mom must have

472
00:32:41,734 --> 00:32:43,870
really badmouthed me from up there, huh?

473
00:32:43,870 --> 00:32:46,461
Given Mom's temper,
do you think she stayed quiet?

474
00:32:54,306 --> 00:32:58,209
Your mom and I had you when we were 20.

475
00:32:58,209 --> 00:33:00,242
We were clueless back then.

476
00:33:01,336 --> 00:33:03,778
Babies raising a baby.

477
00:33:08,370 --> 00:33:11,320
It seems like we raised you, but...

478
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:13,021
- Hey.
- Huh?

479
00:33:13,021 --> 00:33:15,767
you actually turned us into parents

480
00:33:15,767 --> 00:33:16,635
What's the time?

481
00:33:16,635 --> 00:33:18,760
- and made us into adults.
- It's six.

482
00:33:20,801 --> 00:33:22,398
Right here in this place,

483
00:33:22,398 --> 00:33:23,832
Hang on.

484
00:33:23,832 --> 00:33:25,700
both you and I...

485
00:33:26,767 --> 00:33:28,837
we grew up side by side.

486
00:33:32,767 --> 00:33:34,267
Hey.

487
00:33:34,267 --> 00:33:36,046
Do you recall that moment?

488
00:33:36,046 --> 00:33:37,214
When?

489
00:33:37,214 --> 00:33:41,182
Looking up at the sky with me right here.

490
00:33:47,823 --> 00:33:50,895
Dad, where are we heading?

491
00:33:50,895 --> 00:33:52,618
You're up?

492
00:33:52,618 --> 00:33:55,297
Since it's the Lunar New Year,
we have to go to Grandma's.

493
00:34:00,469 --> 00:34:02,204
- Dad.
- What?

494
00:34:02,204 --> 00:34:04,673
Why does the sky look like that?

495
00:34:07,178 --> 00:34:09,912
That is called daybreak.

496
00:34:09,912 --> 00:34:11,190
Daybreak?

497
00:34:11,190 --> 00:34:12,291
Yes.

498
00:34:12,291 --> 00:34:15,391
This must be the first time
you've seen the morning twilight.

499
00:34:15,391 --> 00:34:17,054
Isn't it lovely?

500
00:34:17,054 --> 00:34:19,054
It's gorgeous.

501
00:34:19,757 --> 00:34:20,851
Dad.

502
00:34:20,851 --> 00:34:21,650
Yeah?

503
00:34:21,650 --> 00:34:25,460
Thanks for letting me see the daybreak.

504
00:34:26,797 --> 00:34:28,271
Yeah...

505
00:34:28,271 --> 00:34:29,998
Of course.

506
00:34:31,268 --> 00:34:32,431
Honey.

507
00:34:32,431 --> 00:34:34,031
We'll be late, come on.

508
00:34:34,031 --> 00:34:35,773
Yeah, heading out.

509
00:34:35,773 --> 00:34:36,668
Let's go.

510
00:34:36,668 --> 00:34:38,506
Did you wake up?

511
00:34:48,152 --> 00:34:50,485
Doesn't that weigh a ton?

512
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:55,290
- That belongs to you, right?
- What?

513
00:34:55,290 --> 00:34:56,691
- The backpack?
- Backpack.

514
00:34:57,895 --> 00:34:58,968
- Ja Yeong.
- Yes?

515
00:34:58,968 --> 00:35:01,363
Could you take the top one for me?

516
00:35:12,589 --> 00:35:14,217
- Oh, come on inside.
- Okay, thanks.

517
00:35:14,217 --> 00:35:16,211
That must be heavy.

518
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,337
Jun Kyung.

519
00:35:23,337 --> 00:35:24,486
Yes.

520
00:35:28,158 --> 00:35:31,595
I left your mom's bed untouched,
just like you said.

521
00:35:31,595 --> 00:35:32,694
Okay.

522
00:35:32,694 --> 00:35:34,290
We can use my room,

523
00:35:34,290 --> 00:35:37,499
so we're leaving the master bedroom
and Jun Seo's room alone.

524
00:35:56,883 --> 00:35:58,787
Let's

525
00:35:58,787 --> 00:36:00,467
keep in contact,

526
00:36:00,467 --> 00:36:02,357
meet up often,

527
00:36:02,357 --> 00:36:04,534
and, anyway,

528
00:36:04,534 --> 00:36:06,228
let's all take good care of ourselves.

529
00:36:06,228 --> 00:36:07,429
- Okay, you too, Dad.
- You too.

530
00:36:07,429 --> 00:36:08,597
Stop by the camping site.

531
00:36:08,597 --> 00:36:10,935
- Sure, will do.
- We'll drop by frequently.

532
00:36:10,935 --> 00:36:12,336
- I'm off.
- Okay.

533
00:36:12,336 --> 00:36:14,569
- Drive carefully.
- I'm really leaving.

534
00:36:14,569 --> 00:36:15,464
Drive safely.

535
00:36:15,464 --> 00:36:17,358
- Drive safe, Dad.
- Yes.

536
00:36:24,173 --> 00:36:24,881
We should get going, too.

537
00:36:24,881 --> 00:36:26,195
Man, how should I handle this?

538
00:36:26,195 --> 00:36:28,535
Just send them off. Quit bothering Hye On.

539
00:36:28,535 --> 00:36:30,115
Don't give him a hard time.

540
00:36:30,115 --> 00:36:32,420
- Got it.
- We're leaving.

541
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:40,228
I told you I'd go ahead with the luggage.

542
00:36:40,798 --> 00:36:43,098
What in the world is packed in here?

543
00:36:45,434 --> 00:36:46,901
What the heck is this?

544
00:36:52,910 --> 00:36:54,676
Thank you.

545
00:36:57,501 --> 00:36:59,006
Wait...

546
00:37:09,601 --> 00:37:11,526
Wait, actually...

547
00:37:11,526 --> 00:37:13,695
This piece isn't half bad, is it?

548
00:37:27,248 --> 00:37:28,612
Ja Yeong.

549
00:37:28,612 --> 00:37:29,713
Yeah?

550
00:37:29,713 --> 00:37:31,279
Get out here, quick.

551
00:37:31,279 --> 00:37:32,914
- What's up?
- Come on, hurry up.

552
00:37:32,914 --> 00:37:34,418
- What's going on?
- Hurry up.

553
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:35,989
- It's huge, come on.
- What?

554
00:37:35,989 --> 00:37:37,819
Look right there.

555
00:37:42,934 --> 00:37:45,288
Which part is the circle?

556
00:37:45,288 --> 00:37:48,608
You claimed Corona Borealis was round.

557
00:37:48,608 --> 00:37:51,248
Oh, I must have skipped that detail.

558
00:37:51,248 --> 00:37:53,701
Only good-hearted folks can see it.

559
00:37:56,638 --> 00:37:58,034
Finally over.

560
00:37:58,034 --> 00:38:00,875
What a load off my mind.

561
00:38:06,414 --> 00:38:08,016
Rough day, huh?

562
00:38:14,022 --> 00:38:15,924
Perched here

563
00:38:16,467 --> 00:38:19,227
on the deck of this vintage house...

564
00:38:21,649 --> 00:38:23,932
don't we give off elderly couple vibes?

565
00:38:23,932 --> 00:38:25,236
Elderly couple?

566
00:38:25,236 --> 00:38:26,467
Yes.

567
00:38:27,701 --> 00:38:29,567
You know, the type

568
00:38:29,567 --> 00:38:31,976
who've lived harmoniously under this roof

569
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,608
for three

570
00:38:34,778 --> 00:38:36,344
or four decades

571
00:38:37,581 --> 00:38:39,547
without any real drama.

572
00:38:44,922 --> 00:38:46,701
Care for...

573
00:38:46,701 --> 00:38:48,156
an ice-cold beer?

574
00:38:49,126 --> 00:38:50,425
Deal!

575
00:38:52,863 --> 00:38:55,096
Fill it to the brim with ice.

576
00:38:56,631 --> 00:38:58,101
Okay.

577
00:39:15,116 --> 00:39:16,985
Here's your food.

578
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,560
He's got a good appetite.

579
00:39:26,657 --> 00:39:29,217
Whenever you feel like visiting your dad,
just say the word.

580
00:39:29,217 --> 00:39:30,665
I'll drive you over.

581
00:39:32,223 --> 00:39:34,836
Heading over there right now feels kind of off.

582
00:39:35,482 --> 00:39:37,422
I'm not that oblivious.

583
00:39:37,422 --> 00:39:38,739
How come?

584
00:39:39,543 --> 00:39:40,814
What?

585
00:39:47,151 --> 00:39:48,375
Oh...

586
00:39:49,384 --> 00:39:51,186
Dad...

587
00:39:51,186 --> 00:39:53,888
moved in with Jun Kyung.

588
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:56,658
You didn't know?

589
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:03,899
Let's get some caffeine.

590
00:40:03,899 --> 00:40:06,971
The machine in the pantry is top-notch.

591
00:40:06,971 --> 00:40:09,537
If the hospital coffee is that good,
why did you resign?

592
00:40:13,708 --> 00:40:14,943
By the way...

593
00:40:14,943 --> 00:40:17,913
your family is incredibly trendy.

594
00:40:17,913 --> 00:40:20,081
Young, middle-aged, seniors...

595
00:40:20,081 --> 00:40:22,436
everyone's just living together
instead of tying the knot.

596
00:40:22,951 --> 00:40:24,463
Seriously chic.

597
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:25,820
Totally chill.

598
00:40:26,362 --> 00:40:27,789
Are you dissing me?

599
00:40:29,727 --> 00:40:33,294
Since when is being trendy an insult?

600
00:40:35,472 --> 00:40:38,472
But level with me. Moving in so abruptly...

601
00:40:38,472 --> 00:40:41,149
was that partly because you felt insecure

602
00:40:41,149 --> 00:40:43,017
about that bold new woman
who's stirring things up?

603
00:40:43,834 --> 00:40:44,707
Well...

604
00:40:44,707 --> 00:40:47,909
Maybe killing two birds with one stone
without meaning to?

605
00:40:51,112 --> 00:40:52,113
Got plans later?

606
00:40:52,113 --> 00:40:53,621
I'm hitting up a kids' cafe
with the little ones.

607
00:40:53,621 --> 00:40:55,219
Come along.

608
00:40:55,219 --> 00:40:56,851
Keep dreaming.

609
00:41:01,456 --> 00:41:03,157
Hello.

610
00:41:03,661 --> 00:41:06,027
You're still on your lunch break, right?

611
00:41:10,768 --> 00:41:13,434
Word is you and Do Hyun are living together.

612
00:41:17,682 --> 00:41:21,142
Was that worth showing up at my workplace for?

613
00:41:24,779 --> 00:41:27,281
Well, rather than that...

614
00:41:27,767 --> 00:41:31,619
I was actually curious
if marriage is on the cards.

615
00:41:33,691 --> 00:41:35,890
What makes you ask that?

616
00:41:38,018 --> 00:41:40,095
Someone said this once.

617
00:41:40,095 --> 00:41:42,801
You date, argue,

618
00:41:42,801 --> 00:41:46,234
split up, become strangers, then reconnect...

619
00:41:46,234 --> 00:41:50,304
A husband and wife are the only family
you get to pick.

620
00:41:52,674 --> 00:41:54,003
What are you getting at?

621
00:41:54,003 --> 00:41:55,635
Just saying

622
00:41:55,635 --> 00:41:58,762
it's more complicated than it seems.

623
00:41:58,762 --> 00:42:01,051
Unlike a spouse,
you can't choose your parents or kids,

624
00:42:01,051 --> 00:42:03,184
and you can't cut ties with them.

625
00:42:04,588 --> 00:42:07,422
Do Hyun is Daniel's father.

626
00:42:07,892 --> 00:42:10,491
And I'm his mother.

627
00:42:18,899 --> 00:42:21,367
I'm not sure yet,

628
00:42:21,367 --> 00:42:24,806
but if we do tie the knot,
you'll be the first to know.

629
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:33,100
You know...

630
00:42:33,100 --> 00:42:35,550
whenever we meet,

631
00:42:35,550 --> 00:42:39,120
I get the feeling we're pretty similar.
Don't you agree?

632
00:42:43,391 --> 00:42:44,225
How so?

633
00:42:44,225 --> 00:42:47,902
We both suck at expressing
or concealing our emotions.

634
00:42:47,902 --> 00:42:50,767
We're easily wounded by envy,

635
00:42:50,767 --> 00:42:53,279
run off when we're busted,

636
00:42:53,279 --> 00:42:56,671
and neither of us knows how to say sorry
or take an apology.

637
00:42:57,400 --> 00:42:59,173
Isn't that right?

638
00:43:15,835 --> 00:43:18,225
Whenever we meet,

639
00:43:18,225 --> 00:43:21,729
I get the feeling we're pretty similar.
Don't you agree?

640
00:43:33,644 --> 00:43:35,877
Similar? Give me a break.

641
00:43:46,123 --> 00:43:48,659
You're here. Tough trip, huh?

642
00:43:48,659 --> 00:43:50,959
Thanks for coming all this way.

643
00:43:50,959 --> 00:43:52,841
Right... You guys doing okay?

644
00:43:52,841 --> 00:43:54,162
Thanks for making the trip.

645
00:43:54,162 --> 00:43:56,155
Hello.

646
00:43:56,155 --> 00:43:57,966
Honestly,

647
00:43:57,966 --> 00:44:00,135
you went from being a Chief to a bum,

648
00:44:00,135 --> 00:44:01,801
and now you're a CEO.

649
00:44:01,801 --> 00:44:04,199
Your life is a total roller coaster.

650
00:44:04,199 --> 00:44:05,500
Congrats.

651
00:44:05,500 --> 00:44:08,719
You shouldn't have brought anything.
What is all this?

652
00:44:08,719 --> 00:44:10,445
Ta-da!

653
00:44:10,445 --> 00:44:13,540
I told you to take out the product logo!

654
00:44:13,540 --> 00:44:15,984
"Bom Camping Site, Strike it Rich!"

655
00:44:15,984 --> 00:44:17,479
We appreciate it.

656
00:44:17,479 --> 00:44:19,420
Okay, let's go.

657
00:44:22,359 --> 00:44:24,128
Mind your fingers.

658
00:44:24,128 --> 00:44:25,893
Please, come inside.

659
00:44:26,397 --> 00:44:28,963
The air is so fresh out here.

660
00:44:29,631 --> 00:44:32,200
- This tastes amazing.
- Is it tasty?

661
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:33,134
Please, help yourself to plenty.

662
00:44:33,134 --> 00:44:34,371
Thank you.

663
00:44:34,371 --> 00:44:35,840
Please, have some yourself.

664
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:37,171
Okay.

665
00:44:42,267 --> 00:44:43,644
Cheers!

666
00:44:47,081 --> 00:44:48,316
Are you happy?

667
00:44:48,316 --> 00:44:50,685
I am. I love it.

668
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:55,467
- Don't pick it up with your fingers.
- Try this.

669
00:44:55,467 --> 00:44:58,100
Okay, I'll help myself.

670
00:44:58,100 --> 00:45:00,294
- Ew, gross!
- Just have a bite.

671
00:45:14,278 --> 00:45:15,876
What are you thinking about?

672
00:45:18,782 --> 00:45:20,262
Just...

673
00:45:21,252 --> 00:45:23,453
it's kind of amazing.

674
00:45:24,567 --> 00:45:27,854
How we were total strangers, yet we met...

675
00:45:28,823 --> 00:45:30,995
weathered all that time

676
00:45:30,995 --> 00:45:34,328
and ended up here together.

677
00:45:39,367 --> 00:45:40,701
True.

678
00:45:44,133 --> 00:45:45,473
If you

679
00:45:46,140 --> 00:45:49,010
hadn't made that gutsy confession that day,

680
00:45:50,734 --> 00:45:52,380
we probably

681
00:45:54,873 --> 00:45:57,051
wouldn't be sitting here now, would we?

682
00:45:59,360 --> 00:46:01,749
Me? I was the one who confessed?

683
00:46:03,194 --> 00:46:05,159
Look at you, acting like you have amnesia.

684
00:46:06,294 --> 00:46:09,263
You don't recall

685
00:46:09,971 --> 00:46:13,668
what you said
when you rang my doorbell that day?

686
00:46:14,702 --> 00:46:16,371
What exactly did I say?

687
00:46:16,371 --> 00:46:18,955
Wait, I'm pretty sure that wasn't a confession.

688
00:46:18,955 --> 00:46:20,374
Oh my.

689
00:46:21,511 --> 00:46:23,411
You really don't remember.

690
00:46:23,411 --> 00:46:26,881
I, on the other hand, remember everything,

691
00:46:26,881 --> 00:46:30,287
right down to your outfit and shoes.

692
00:46:30,287 --> 00:46:32,119
No way.

693
00:46:34,669 --> 00:46:37,892
A white shirt with a huge collar like wings...

694
00:46:37,892 --> 00:46:40,167
white trousers...

695
00:46:40,167 --> 00:46:41,696
And you must have been in a hurry...

696
00:46:41,696 --> 00:46:44,133
you practically flew to my door

697
00:46:44,133 --> 00:46:46,011
in your slippers.

698
00:46:46,011 --> 00:46:48,111
Like a little cherub.

699
00:46:48,111 --> 00:46:50,638
That gave me chills.

700
00:46:52,763 --> 00:46:56,723
Is there anything about you I don't know?

701
00:46:56,723 --> 00:46:59,167
I watch,

702
00:46:59,167 --> 00:47:00,948
analyze,

703
00:47:01,801 --> 00:47:03,350
and study you daily...

704
00:47:04,052 --> 00:47:06,087
I am the foremost

705
00:47:06,087 --> 00:47:07,955
expert on Seo Jun Kyung.

706
00:47:08,423 --> 00:47:10,727
So you're the authority on me.

707
00:47:15,363 --> 00:47:17,164
What's wrong?

708
00:47:19,267 --> 00:47:20,435
Sitting

709
00:47:20,435 --> 00:47:22,835
at a desk all day is

710
00:47:22,835 --> 00:47:24,901
- killing my lower back, right here.
- Your back is acting up?

711
00:47:24,901 --> 00:47:26,708
Right there.

712
00:47:26,708 --> 00:47:27,556
Here?

713
00:47:27,556 --> 00:47:28,476
Oh, that's the spot.

714
00:47:28,476 --> 00:47:31,916
If you're in pain, shouldn't it hurt more
when I press it like this?

715
00:47:31,916 --> 00:47:34,215
- Oh, I love it.
- Does it hurt even more now?

716
00:47:34,215 --> 00:47:38,319
I figured throwing a housewarming party

717
00:47:38,319 --> 00:47:42,256
was just something everyone did.
Turns out, not really.

718
00:47:43,508 --> 00:47:45,259
What are you saying?

719
00:47:46,173 --> 00:47:50,868
It feels like I'm flaunting
that I'm doing well,

720
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:55,236
or maybe swearing to myself
that I'll live even better from now on.

721
00:47:56,013 --> 00:47:58,234
Even though I'm not sure

722
00:47:58,234 --> 00:48:00,141
what "living well" really means.

723
00:48:01,013 --> 00:48:03,978
Living well means...

724
00:48:05,380 --> 00:48:07,615
using a towel

725
00:48:07,615 --> 00:48:10,985
on your face

726
00:48:10,985 --> 00:48:13,354
when it's plush and soft,

727
00:48:13,354 --> 00:48:16,400
then on your feet

728
00:48:16,400 --> 00:48:19,026
when the threads come loose
and it gets scratchy.

729
00:48:19,554 --> 00:48:24,064
And when it's stained and stretched out
even after you boil it...

730
00:48:24,534 --> 00:48:27,134
using it as a rag.

731
00:48:29,370 --> 00:48:31,772
Living like that

732
00:48:32,507 --> 00:48:35,276
is living well.

733
00:48:38,901 --> 00:48:41,282
Thanks for coming.

734
00:48:43,587 --> 00:48:45,553
I really mean it.

735
00:48:49,693 --> 00:48:51,458
Ja Yeong.

736
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:18,953
♪ Let's live a good life ♪

737
00:49:18,953 --> 00:49:22,153
♪ Let's live a good life ♪

738
00:49:22,153 --> 00:49:24,695
♪ Let's give it a shot ♪

739
00:49:24,695 --> 00:49:27,228
♪ Let's live a good life ♪

740
00:49:28,666 --> 00:49:31,232
♪ Let's live a good life ♪

741
00:49:31,232 --> 00:49:33,237
♪ Let's live a good life ♪

742
00:49:33,237 --> 00:49:35,703
She's tipsy.

743
00:49:37,238 --> 00:49:39,406
Just drunk all by herself.

744
00:49:56,224 --> 00:49:57,892
Hold on.

745
00:49:57,892 --> 00:49:59,968
Hey... what are you...

746
00:49:59,968 --> 00:50:00,865
what are you doing?

747
00:50:00,865 --> 00:50:02,552
I've been dying to try this...

748
00:50:02,552 --> 00:50:03,764
Try what?

749
00:50:06,267 --> 00:50:07,171
Huh?

750
00:50:07,171 --> 00:50:08,969
Come home early, darling.

751
00:50:11,075 --> 00:50:12,612
Come on.

752
00:50:12,612 --> 00:50:15,409
We look like newlyweds.

753
00:50:16,380 --> 00:50:18,415
This outfit is ancient.

754
00:50:18,415 --> 00:50:20,281
Is this the only one you've got?

755
00:50:21,085 --> 00:50:24,118
When would I ever need a suit?

756
00:50:24,629 --> 00:50:27,258
I guess it shows how I've spent
my life up until now.

757
00:50:27,258 --> 00:50:29,501
Once I bag that award cash,

758
00:50:29,501 --> 00:50:31,434
I'll get you a tie...

759
00:50:31,434 --> 00:50:32,660
no...

760
00:50:33,327 --> 00:50:34,990
a full suit.

761
00:50:34,990 --> 00:50:36,534
Something high-end.

762
00:50:36,534 --> 00:50:40,100
Listen to you, spending money
you haven't even won.

763
00:50:41,305 --> 00:50:43,234
When I become a novelist

764
00:50:43,234 --> 00:50:45,634
and you're a professor,

765
00:50:45,634 --> 00:50:47,578
should we get hitched?

766
00:50:47,578 --> 00:50:49,610
What? You're making me blush.

767
00:50:49,610 --> 00:50:51,048
Stop it, cut it out.

768
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:53,617
Knock them dead.

769
00:50:53,617 --> 00:50:54,451
Yeah.

770
00:50:54,451 --> 00:50:56,250
- I won't let you down.
- Yes.

771
00:50:57,518 --> 00:50:59,353
- I'll be in touch.
- Yes.

772
00:50:59,353 --> 00:51:01,622
- Go for it!
- Yeah.

773
00:51:03,925 --> 00:51:07,098
The professor already smoothed things over,
so don't worry.

774
00:51:07,098 --> 00:51:09,944
Right. Don't panic. Just answer clearly,

775
00:51:09,944 --> 00:51:12,333
"Yes! Yes!" to whatever they ask.

776
00:51:12,333 --> 00:51:13,605
Panic? Please...

777
00:51:13,605 --> 00:51:14,939
Okay. Good luck.

778
00:51:14,939 --> 00:51:16,804
You got this! Don't get nervous.

779
00:51:16,804 --> 00:51:18,442
I told you, I'm not nervous.

780
00:51:18,442 --> 00:51:19,673
Alright.

781
00:51:21,011 --> 00:51:23,310
He sounded nervous.

782
00:51:40,328 --> 00:51:42,085
Jin Ho.

783
00:51:42,085 --> 00:51:43,998
Jin Ho, look at this.

784
00:51:43,998 --> 00:51:47,057
There are tons of aralia shoots up there.

785
00:51:47,057 --> 00:51:48,635
Take a look at...

786
00:51:53,110 --> 00:51:54,508
Right.

787
00:51:55,846 --> 00:51:57,911
My gosh. What's wrong with me?

788
00:52:05,723 --> 00:52:07,537
You did an internship
at a broadcasting station.

789
00:52:07,537 --> 00:52:10,267
- Ah, yes!
- Your thesis was approved.

790
00:52:10,267 --> 00:52:11,458
Yes.

791
00:52:12,927 --> 00:52:15,398
And you graduate if you complete
just six credits this semester?

792
00:52:15,398 --> 00:52:17,257
Yes. That's right.

793
00:52:17,257 --> 00:52:20,167
But your undergrad GPA is not great,
so why is that?

794
00:52:21,268 --> 00:52:22,736
Ah...

795
00:52:23,270 --> 00:52:27,558
well... I was going through
some personal stuff back then.

796
00:52:27,558 --> 00:52:28,957
What kind of stuff?

797
00:52:28,957 --> 00:52:30,411
Well...

798
00:52:31,481 --> 00:52:33,280
I'm not actually asking.

799
00:52:33,280 --> 00:52:34,749
Yes.

800
00:52:34,749 --> 00:52:37,418
Professor Song recommended you

801
00:52:37,418 --> 00:52:39,890
and we have a vacancy
for a liberal arts instructor.

802
00:52:39,890 --> 00:52:42,635
So you wouldn't be a bad fit for the position.

803
00:52:42,635 --> 00:52:44,125
But there's a protocol.

804
00:52:44,125 --> 00:52:47,198
I'll speak with the department head
and contact you shortly.

805
00:52:47,198 --> 00:52:48,532
Ah, yes.

806
00:52:48,532 --> 00:52:50,064
Thank you.

807
00:52:54,626 --> 00:52:56,203
Jin Ho,

808
00:52:56,901 --> 00:52:58,872
are you still fuming?

809
00:53:00,307 --> 00:53:01,468
It's not about being mad.

810
00:53:01,468 --> 00:53:04,982
It's just that a fire in these mountains
would be a disaster.

811
00:53:04,982 --> 00:53:07,714
You're right.
It really could have been a disaster.

812
00:53:08,649 --> 00:53:10,916
Maybe I got too carried away moving here.

813
00:53:10,916 --> 00:53:12,586
I'm so out of it.

814
00:53:13,261 --> 00:53:15,059
I'm truly sorry.

815
00:53:15,059 --> 00:53:18,158
I promise, really,
I'll keep my head on straight from now on.

816
00:53:20,081 --> 00:53:21,955
Well, if you're happy enough here

817
00:53:21,955 --> 00:53:25,065
to lose your mind, that's fortunate.

818
00:53:27,404 --> 00:53:30,537
Does that mean you're not angry anymore?

819
00:53:31,475 --> 00:53:33,373
No, I'm still holding a grudge.

820
00:53:34,303 --> 00:53:35,202
Oh, don't be like that!

821
00:53:35,202 --> 00:53:36,944
Stop it.

822
00:53:39,991 --> 00:53:41,272
No tickling.

823
00:53:41,272 --> 00:53:43,287
I'm not over it, so shoo.

824
00:53:43,287 --> 00:53:44,685
Stop it.

825
00:53:45,723 --> 00:53:47,154
No.

826
00:53:49,356 --> 00:53:53,460
Do you know what matters more
than the diamond in a proposal?

827
00:53:54,298 --> 00:53:55,696
What is that?

828
00:53:56,233 --> 00:53:57,664
The right moment.

829
00:53:58,291 --> 00:54:00,134
Too cliche?

830
00:54:00,134 --> 00:54:03,938
It's not about your schedule,
or even 'our' schedule as a couple.

831
00:54:03,938 --> 00:54:06,573
It has to be a moment
that belongs entirely to her.

832
00:54:07,463 --> 00:54:09,680
But how on earth could you predict that?

833
00:54:09,680 --> 00:54:11,445
That's the tricky part.

834
00:54:19,056 --> 00:54:21,792
I told you, taking the academy bus
would've been fine.

835
00:54:21,792 --> 00:54:23,561
I've got nothing else to do.

836
00:54:23,561 --> 00:54:25,359
You know I'm out of work.

837
00:54:26,997 --> 00:54:28,365
Then go find a job.

838
00:54:28,365 --> 00:54:32,199
How about you ditch class
and we go grab some tteokbokki?

839
00:54:33,200 --> 00:54:36,371
Why not just quit the academy altogether
and hang out with me?

840
00:54:36,371 --> 00:54:39,139
How can I just quit?

841
00:54:39,774 --> 00:54:41,520
You really aren't

842
00:54:41,520 --> 00:54:43,590
like the other moms.

843
00:54:43,590 --> 00:54:47,114
So, you wish I acted like them?

844
00:54:47,818 --> 00:54:49,320
Nah,

845
00:54:49,320 --> 00:54:50,493
I'd hate that.

846
00:54:53,334 --> 00:54:54,688
But...

847
00:54:56,302 --> 00:54:58,392
aren't you gonna start seeing anyone?

848
00:54:59,530 --> 00:55:00,827
Why do you ask?

849
00:55:02,290 --> 00:55:03,797
I mean...

850
00:55:04,957 --> 00:55:06,570
Just because

851
00:55:06,570 --> 00:55:08,917
Dad has a girlfriend.

852
00:55:08,917 --> 00:55:11,437
You used to hate the idea of me dating.

853
00:55:11,437 --> 00:55:13,514
You wanted the three of us,

854
00:55:13,514 --> 00:55:16,710
you, Dad, and me, just to live together.

855
00:55:17,211 --> 00:55:18,478
That's ancient history.

856
00:55:18,478 --> 00:55:20,284
I was basically a baby.

857
00:55:20,284 --> 00:55:21,715
What about now?

858
00:55:22,353 --> 00:55:25,185
Do you want me to find a guy?

859
00:55:26,453 --> 00:55:28,055
I just

860
00:55:30,067 --> 00:55:32,326
don't want you to be by yourself.

861
00:55:35,266 --> 00:55:37,231
Do I seem lonely?

862
00:55:40,367 --> 00:55:41,668
Well...

863
00:55:43,174 --> 00:55:44,671
Maybe a tiny bit.

864
00:55:48,379 --> 00:55:49,543
Alright then.

865
00:55:49,543 --> 00:55:51,979
I'll make an effort not to be lonely.

866
00:55:55,212 --> 00:55:56,929
I'm in a jam.

867
00:55:56,929 --> 00:55:59,268
The recording isn't going anywhere,

868
00:55:59,268 --> 00:56:00,775
so it looks
like I'll be stuck here for a while.

869
00:56:00,775 --> 00:56:02,055
Really?

870
00:56:02,055 --> 00:56:04,324
I was just whipping up some curry.

871
00:56:05,690 --> 00:56:08,028
I'm so exhausted today.

872
00:56:09,033 --> 00:56:11,298
Curry made by the one I love...

873
00:56:11,866 --> 00:56:13,563
Today was the perfect day for that.

874
00:56:14,935 --> 00:56:17,104
I guess our timing is off.

875
00:56:35,983 --> 00:56:37,270
It's him!

876
00:56:43,467 --> 00:56:44,598
Hello, Professor.

877
00:56:44,598 --> 00:56:47,167
Everything's sorted out.

878
00:56:47,167 --> 00:56:49,173
We're locking you in
for the class next semester.

879
00:56:49,173 --> 00:56:50,870
Really?

880
00:56:50,870 --> 00:56:53,474
Let's test the waters for a semester.

881
00:56:53,474 --> 00:56:55,613
If the kids dig it, we'll keep you on.

882
00:56:55,613 --> 00:56:57,377
Thank you so much.

883
00:56:58,010 --> 00:57:00,014
- Oh, and one more thing.
- Yes.

884
00:57:00,014 --> 00:57:02,149
You just need to have 5 million ready.

885
00:57:04,535 --> 00:57:05,835
Excuse me?

886
00:57:06,320 --> 00:57:10,224
Lots of lecturers are eyeing
those general electives,

887
00:57:10,224 --> 00:57:12,033
and the complaints are endless.

888
00:57:12,033 --> 00:57:14,100
As long as you have that amount ready,
you should be fine.

889
00:57:14,100 --> 00:57:15,929
Su Jin mentioned

890
00:57:17,097 --> 00:57:19,234
that this spring feels particularly bitter

891
00:57:19,234 --> 00:57:21,067
Right...

892
00:57:21,067 --> 00:57:22,234
and cruel.

893
00:57:22,234 --> 00:57:24,137
Then by when do I need to...

894
00:57:25,372 --> 00:57:29,142
Come to think of it,
we have the wrong idea about spring.

895
00:57:30,477 --> 00:57:32,713
With warm sunshine

896
00:57:34,033 --> 00:57:38,151
that is neither too hot nor too cold,
it seems like such a pleasant season.

897
00:57:39,453 --> 00:57:43,123
It acts kindly, making us let our guard down.

898
00:57:45,359 --> 00:57:48,762
But spring is not actually that benevolent.

899
00:57:50,230 --> 00:57:51,250
Thanks a lot.

900
00:57:51,250 --> 00:57:52,411
No problem. Enjoy your break.

901
00:57:52,411 --> 00:57:53,870
Thank you.

902
00:57:53,870 --> 00:57:55,335
Bye.

903
00:57:56,373 --> 00:57:59,276
I thought only warmer days were ahead.

904
00:57:59,276 --> 00:58:00,290
Yeah, Ja Yeong?

905
00:58:00,290 --> 00:58:02,870
Have you seen our Bom?

906
00:58:02,870 --> 00:58:07,681
But sometimes an unexpected cold snap
returns to surprise us.

907
00:58:07,681 --> 00:58:10,117
I can't see Bom anywhere.

908
00:58:11,470 --> 00:58:13,019
Bom.

909
00:58:13,958 --> 00:58:16,022
Bom, where are you?

910
00:58:17,500 --> 00:58:21,495
The unstable air creates
severe temperature swings,

911
00:58:24,998 --> 00:58:27,868
and the differing faces of day and night

912
00:58:29,501 --> 00:58:32,672
catch us off guard.

913
00:58:34,661 --> 00:58:37,811
Confusing us with a colorless

914
00:58:39,601 --> 00:58:42,616
and shimmering haze,

915
00:58:44,651 --> 00:58:46,219
spring is

916
00:58:47,901 --> 00:58:49,823
passing by again

917
00:58:51,634 --> 00:58:53,660
this year,

918
00:58:55,868 --> 00:58:57,864
leaving us anything but safe.
